course: dictionary
lesson: 14200
title: Big words for big places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mountainous means having many mountains. A mountainous country has lots of mountains, so you can often see peaks from almost anywhere in it. «The village sits in a mountainous region of Nepal, far from the nearest city.» The word tells you the land is covered with mountains.
explain: Mountainous can also mean huge. «The mountainous waves crashed over the little boat in the storm.» Waves cannot really be mountains, so the word means enormous, as big as mountains. Check by swapping in huge: «The huge waves crashed over the little boat» still makes sense.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Look at the nouns around the word: a country, a region, or waves. A country is a place, so mountainous means full of mountains. Waves are water, so mountainous means huge and dangerous.
fact: Mountainous is an adjective, a word that describes a place or thing.
fact: «Mountainous» means having many mountains.
fact: «Mountainous» can also mean huge, as in «mountainous waves».
fact: Mountainous countries, such as Switzerland, Nepal and the Scottish Highlands, are often cold, with fewer roads and towns.
fact: In stories, mountainous waves show a dangerous storm.
exercise: «Many people visit the mountainous country of Switzerland.» What does mountainous mean here? | Flat and sandy | Full of shops and busy streets | Very small | *Having many mountains
exercise: «The mountainous waves crashed against the ship.» What does mountainous suggest about the waves? | Calm and still | *Huge and dangerous | Quiet and slow | Warm and pretty
exercise: Which place is most likely to be mountainous? | *The Scottish Highlands | A sandy beach in a busy city | A school playground | A flat field in the fens
test: Why might a mountainous region have fewer towns than a flat region? | Mountains are always full of shops | Mountains have no weather at all | Towns prefer to be on mountains | *Steep mountains make roads and buildings hard to build
test: «The storm brought mountainous waves to the harbour.» Which word is closest in meaning to mountainous here? | *Enormous | Quiet | Tiny | Gentle
exam: Jo reads «the mountainous waves tossed the boat» and wonders what mountainous means. What should she do first? | Skip the sentence and never read it again | Guess that it means happy | *Swap in a word such as huge and see if the sentence still makes sense | Ask someone to write the answer for her
